{"additions":3831,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nA new read-only **Docker** page (`4`) for vig, built only on the `docker` CLI's JSON output (`docker version / ps / images / inspect / logs`). It lists containers grouped by compose project, local images, an inspect summary for the selection, and a live log tail. Nothing in the page mutates state, and environment variables are never displayed (the inspect structs have no `Env` field, so they are never even deserialized).\n\n![docker demo](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/td72/vig/feat/docker-view/assets/demo-docker.gif)\n\nCloses #87, closes #88, closes #89, closes #90, closes #91, closes #92\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Page skeleton (#88)** — `src/docker/{page,state,domain,panes}`, registered as the 4th page in `main.rs`; `page \"docker\"` block in `assets/default.kdl` (left column: containers / images, right column: detail / logs; `tabs`, `bind`, per-pane keys) and `\"4\" \"page:docker\"` in `app {}`; `Config::docker_page()` + loader test; `docker version --format json` detection on first activation with a \"docker not available\" notice replacing the panes; background `mpsc` fetch plumbing drained in `drain_background()`.\n- **Containers pane (#89)** — `docker ps -a --format '{{json .}}'`, sorted running-first then by name, nested under synthetic `com.docker.compose.project` rows with `core::tree::nest_by`; state icon, name, image, ports, status; `/` searches name / image; `r` and a 5 s tick refresh the lists; selection drives the detail and logs panes.\n- **Images pane (#90)** — `docker images --format '{{json .}}'`: `repo:tag`, short id, size, relative age; dangling `<none>` images dimmed at the end; `/` searches repository / tag / id; selecting an image shows its inspect summary.\n- **Detail pane (#91)** — `docker inspect` deserialized into purpose-built structs (container: id, name, image, created, state / health / exit code, restart policy, cmd / entrypoint, mounts, ports, networks, labels; image: id, tags, digests, created, size, platform, cmd / entrypoint / workdir, exposed ports, labels), rendered as key/value sections with the GitHub-detail styling; scrollable; in-memory cache, refreshed silently on the list tick. Compose project rows show a member summary.\n- **Logs pane + shared tail component (#92)** — new `core::ui::tail_pane` (`TailState` capped scrollback with follow mode — manual scroll pauses, `G` resumes — half-page navigation, search as list-entry matches; `TailPane` renderer with highlights and a line formatter). The Docker logs pane fetches `docker logs --tail 200 --timestamps`, then `--since <last timestamp>` every second while a container is selected; stdout / stderr are interleaved by timestamp and ANSI escapes stripped.\n- **Docs / demo** — README (en / ja) feature bullet, view-switch row and key table; `docs/config.md` page + actions; `CLAUDE.md` architecture refresh and a \"How to add a page\" checklist; `tape/demo-docker.tape` + `assets/demo-docker.gif`, `mise run demo:docker` (added to `demo:all`).\n\n## Not verified\n\n- Only tested against Docker Engine 27.5 / CLI 29.7 on macOS (lima). Other daemons (Podman's docker shim, rootless, Windows) were not tried.\n- The \"docker not available\" notice was exercised only through the `docker version` error path; not with a missing binary on `PATH`.\n- Help overlays of the Git / GitHub / Files pages still say `1 / 2 / 3` for view switching (left untouched to keep this PR scoped to the new page).\n- The list refresh interval (5 s) and log poll interval (1 s) are constants, not KDL-configurable, because the page block parser rejects unknown nodes and extending it felt out of scope.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w\n","changedFiles":25,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-28T07:53:22Z","deletions":10,"headRefName":"feat/docker-view","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":111,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPKXNA","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe new code uses `Option::is_none_or`, which can unintentionally bump the crate’s MSRV and break builds on older Rust toolchains unless adjusted or the MSRV is pinned.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nAdds a new read-only **Docker** page to vig (registered as view `4`) that uses the `docker` CLI’s JSON output to present containers (grouped by compose project), images, an inspect-summary detail pane, and a live log-tail pane backed by a reusable `TailState`/`TailPane` component.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Introduces `src/docker/` page/state/domain/panes to fetch and render containers, images, inspect summaries, and tailed logs (read-only commands only).\n- Adds a reusable core UI component `core::ui::tail_pane` for capped scrollback + follow/paused mode + search highlighting.\n- Updates built-in config (`assets/default.kdl`), docs (EN/JA + config schema), demo tape/GIF, and demo tasks to include the Docker view.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| tape/demo-docker.tape | New VHS demo tape showcasing Docker view interactions. |\r\n| src/main.rs | Registers the Docker page as the 4th page. |\r\n| src/docker/state.rs | Docker page state, background fetch plumbing, refresh/tick logic, help bindings. |\r\n| src/docker/panes/mod.rs | Exposes Docker panes (containers/detail/images/logs). |\r\n| src/docker/panes/logs.rs | Logs pane: polling, follow/paused behavior via TailState, log rendering/search. |\r\n| src/docker/panes/images.rs | Images list pane with sorting, selection retention, and search. |\r\n| src/docker/panes/detail.rs | Detail pane rendering for container/image inspect summaries and compose project summaries. |\r\n| src/docker/panes/containers.rs | Containers list pane with compose-project grouping/tree layout and search. |\r\n| src/docker/page.rs | Constructs the Docker page (`Page::new(DockerState)`). |\r\n| src/docker/mod.rs | Wires docker module structure (page/panes/state/domain). |\r\n| src/docker/domain/types.rs | Serde types for `docker ps/images/inspect` output (deliberately excluding Env). |\r\n| src/docker/domain/mod.rs | Domain module exports. |\r\n| src/docker/domain/client.rs | Docker CLI command wrappers + parsing helpers (json lines, inspect array, logs merge/strip). |\r\n| src/core/ui/tail_pane.rs | New reusable tail component: capped buffer, follow mode, nav + search integration, renderer. |\r\n| src/core/ui/status_bar.rs | Adds Docker header + status bar rendering (counts, errors, updating indicator). |\r\n| src/core/ui/mod.rs | Exposes `tail_pane` module. |\r\n| src/core/config/loader.rs | Adds `Config::docker_page()` + validation and loader tests; updates app keymap test list. |\r\n| src/core/app.rs | Updates app keymap test to include the Docker page (binding `4`). |\r\n| README.md | Documents Docker view feature, view-switching key, and Docker key table. |\r\n| mise.toml | Adds `demo:docker` task and includes it in `demo:all`. |\r\n| docs/README.ja.md | Japanese docs for Docker view and view switching. |\r\n| docs/config.md | Adds docker page to schema docs and action tables. |\r\n| CLAUDE.md | Updates architecture overview + “How to add a page” checklist to include Docker page/template. |\r\n| assets/demo-docker.gif | Adds Docker demo GIF (Git LFS pointer). |\r\n| assets/default.kdl | Adds docker page layout/tabs/bindings/keymaps and `app` key `4`. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (2)\n\n**src/docker/panes/detail.rs:478**\n* This clones the full labels map on every render. Borrowing `labels` avoids repeated allocations in the detail pane render loop.\n```\n    lines.push(Line::default());\n    let labels = c.config.labels.clone().unwrap_or_default();\n    lines.push(section(&format!(\"Labels ({})\", labels.len())));\n    for (k, v) in &labels {\n        lines.push(item(format!(\"{k}={v}\")));\n```\n**src/docker/panes/detail.rs:462**\n* This clones the entire `Networks` map on every render. Borrowing the map avoids repeated allocations and unnecessary copies when re-rendering the detail pane.\n```\n    lines.push(Line::default());\n    let networks = c.network_settings.networks.clone().unwrap_or_default();\n    lines.push(section(&format!(\"Networks ({})\", networks.len())));\n    for (name, n) in &networks {\n        let ip = if n.ip_address.is_empty() {\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 25/25 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 3\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T07:57:19Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"522649765b6cb4d50b940b68043b249114a5d0d2"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPNXjA","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe log-follow implementation can drop lines because `docker logs` is invoked with `--tail` even when using `--since` for follow polls.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 25/25 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 2\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T08:03:32Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"522649765b6cb4d50b940b68043b249114a5d0d2"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPTyqg","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T08:15:45Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"a8e70176d14908109f274dff45b60e04f3772466"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPTz0g","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T08:15:47Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"a8e70176d14908109f274dff45b60e04f3772466"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPT1JA","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T08:15:49Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"a8e70176d14908109f274dff45b60e04f3772466"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPV4Lg","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🔵 Needs a closer look\n\nIn-app help for the existing Git/GitHub/Files pages still advertises view switching as “1 / 2 / 3” even though a 4th page is now registered, so the UI help is inconsistent with the actual bindings.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (2)\n\n**Previously missed (1)** — in code that hasn't changed since the last review.\n\n**src/core/app.rs:274**\n* Now that a 4th page is registered (Docker), the help overlays for the existing pages still advertise view switching as \"1 / 2 / 3\". This is user-visible and inconsistent with `assets/default.kdl`/README (and Docker’s own help), e.g. `src/git/state.rs:428`, `src/github/state.rs:504`, `src/files/state.rs:343`.\n\nPlease update those pages’ `help_bindings()` first entry to \"1 / 2 / 3 / 4\" so the in-app help matches the actual bindings.\n```\n        let docker_page = crate::docker::page::new_page(&cfg).expect(\"docker page\");\n        let pages = vec![git_page, gh_page, files_page, docker_page];\n\n```\n\n**src/docker/domain/client.rs:157**\n* `merge_log_streams` allocates a new `String` for every timestamp comparison (`to_string()`) and clones log lines into `out` even though the function owns the `Vec<String>`s. This adds unnecessary allocations during every log poll.\n\nYou can avoid both by comparing timestamp slices (`&str`) and by merging via `into_iter().peekable()` so lines are moved into `out` without cloning.\n```\n    let key = |l: &str| split_timestamp(l).0.unwrap_or(\"\").to_string();\n    let (mut i, mut j) = (0, 0);\n    let mut out = Vec::with_capacity(a.len() + b.len());\n    while i < a.len() && j < b.len() {\n        if key(&b[j]) < key(&a[i]) {\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 25/25 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 0 new\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T08:20:31Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"a8e70176d14908109f274dff45b60e04f3772466"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:17:24Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33154752341/job/98794753363","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:17:24Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:17:11Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33154633481/job/98794365270","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:15:39Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:16:22Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions